BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 678 Tm (1. Check extent ordering, logical coverage and tree depth. Overlapping physical extents) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 661.5 Tm (or conflicting ownership must be distinguished from valid shared metadata cases.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 635 Tm (2. An extent marked unwritten is not equivalent to a hole: it has allocated storage but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 618.5 Tm (returns zeroed logical content until initialized.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 592 Tm (3. Verify that the descriptor, bitmap, inode and superblock checksum algorithms match the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 575.5 Tm (exact enabled feature set before declaring corruption.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 549 Tm (4. Journal replay must honour transaction sequence, commits, revokes and checksum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 532.5 Tm (versions. Arbitrary byte-order substitution is unsafe.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 506 Tm (5. Large-file, huge-file, inline-data, bigalloc and flex-group features each alter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 489.5 Tm (interpretation; support cannot be inferred from a generic ext4 label.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 463 Tm (6. Check compatibility masks before writing to an image produced by a newer kernel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 446.5 Tm (Readability does not imply that unknown state can be preserved by the writer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 420 Tm (7. Recovery should distinguish journal replay, bitmap reconciliation and inode/directory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 403.5 Tm (repair rather than treating them as one operation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 377 Tm (8. Record unsupported filesystem revisions or feature combinations explicitly; silently) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 360.5 Tm (discarding unknown metadata undermines cross-platform compatibility.) Tj ET
